akers. [Data: Entities (15840, 15841), Relationships (20246)]", "# Teofilina and High-Protein Diet Interaction\n\nThis community focuses on the interaction between the medication Teofilina and a high-protein diet, highlighting how dietary factors can influence the metabolism and effectiveness of Teofilina in treating respiratory diseases. The relationship between these entities underscores the importance of nutritional considerations in pharmacotherapy.\n\n## Teofilina's therapeutic role in respiratory diseases\n\nTeofilina is primarily used to treat respiratory diseases such as asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). Its effectiveness can be significantly influenced by various factors, including diet. Understanding the pharmacodynamics of Teofilina is crucial for healthcare providers to optimize treatment plans for patients suffering from these conditions. [Data: Entities (14301)]\n\n## Impact of high-protein diet on Teofilina metabolism\n\nA high-protein diet can lead to increased production of cytochrome P450 enzymes, which are responsible for the metabolism of Teofilina. This interaction can result in faster metabolism of the medication, potentially reducing its therapeutic effects. It is essential for healthcare professionals to consider dietary habits when prescribing Teofilina to ensure effective management of respiratory diseases. [Data: Entities (14319); Relationships (19860)]\n\n## Relevance of enteral nutrition in Teofilina administration\n\nThe metabolism of Teofilina can be affected by a diet rich in proteins, particularly in the context of enteral nutrition. This relationship highlights the importance of nutritional management in patients receiving Teofilina, especially those who may be on specialized diets. Understanding these interactions can help in tailoring treatment strategies that consider both medication and nutrition. [Data: Relationships (2796)]\n\n## Clinical implications of dietary interactions with medications\n\nThe inter